              +49 7435 7519 700
            </a>
          </div>

          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-6 gap-y-2 text-sm text-gray-400">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-4 h-4 text-primary" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Specialist in modular laboratory construction</div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-4 h-4 text-primary" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Award 2026 EU Business News</div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-4 h-4 text-primary" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Albstadt works – 80 km</div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-4 h-4 text-primary" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>Wesemann Group · 60+ years of laboratory construction</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <AuthorBio city="Stuttgart"  locale="en" />


    <!-- PATTERN-INTERRUPT: LABtoGO -->
    <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-gradient-to-br from-primary/5 via-white to-primary/10 border-y border-primary/20">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 items-center mb-10">
            <div>
              <div class="text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Pattern interrupt · World premiere at analytica 2026</div>
              <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-4 text-slate-900">Planexus shows Stuttgart what a lab container in 2026 can really do</h2>
              <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                A conventional lab container has 2,400 mm internal height. You can stand up inside — but working upright at a fume cupboard is barely possible.
              </p>
              <p class="text-lg text-slate-900 font-bold leading-relaxed mb-4">
                Planexus LABtoGO has 2,750 mm internal height. 9.5 m external length. 3 m external width. A fully glazed front that brings real daylight into every Stuttgart factory or research laboratory.
              </p>
              <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
                <strong>A conventional lab container fits entirely inside a LABtoGO.</strong> We do not call it LABtoGO without reason — it is the platform on which we configure BSL-2, BSL-3, GMP cleanroom and ATEX for Stuttgart.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 text-center">
                <div class="text-4xl font-bold text-primary mb-1">2.750</div>
                <div class="text-xs text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">mm internal height</div>
                <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">Standard: 2,400 mm</div>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 text-center">
                <div class="text-4xl font-bold text-primary mb-1">9.500</div>
                <div class="text-xs text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">mm external length</div>
                <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">3,000 mm width</div>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 text-center">
                <div class="text-4xl font-bold text-primary mb-1">100%</div>
                <div class="text-xs text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">fully glazed</div>
                <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">daylight laboratory</div>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 text-center">
                <div class="text-4xl font-bold text-primary mb-1">U 0.20</div>
                <div class="text-xs text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wider">W/m²K Sandwich</div>
                <div class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1">80–120 mm insulation</div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="text-center">
            <a href="/en/lab-containers/labtogo" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-primary font-bold hover:underline">
              View the LABtoGO platform and all configurations
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="w-5 h-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PROBLEM-AGITATION -->
    <section class="py-16 md:py-20">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-10 text-slate-900">
            Planexus solves the three Stuttgart bottlenecks at which laboratory projects regularly fail
          </h2>
          <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
            <div class="bg-slate-50 border-l-4 border-primary rounded-xl p-6">
              <div class="text-slate-900 font-bold text-lg mb-2">The funding window closes faster than construction starts</div>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">The funding window of your third-party-funded project closes in nine months. Conventional laboratory construction in Baden-Württemberg takes eighteen to thirty months from building application to keys. You lose the project before it starts.</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-900 font-semibold mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-gray-200">Planexus response: LABtoGO as a modular platform instead of conventional construction.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-slate-50 border-l-4 border-primary rounded-xl p-6">
              <div class="text-slate-900 font-bold text-lg mb-2">Section 50 LBO BW – one formal error costs six weeks</div>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">The Building Code of Baden-Württemberg, the notification procedure (Kenntnisgabeverfahren) and, where applicable, a notification under the Federal Immission Control Act (BImSchG) demand fully review-ready building documents. A single error at the Stuttgart Building Law Office means weeks of standstill.</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-900 font-semibold mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-gray-200">Planexus response: Procedure-ready building documents from day 1.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-slate-50 border-l-4 border-primary rounded-xl p-6">
              <div class="text-slate-900 font-bold text-lg mb-2">Basin-climate reality destroys standard containers</div>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">Inversion weather, summer heat periods above 35 °C, clay soil on the Filder plain and the Stuttgart environmental zone with a green-sticker requirement. Off-the-shelf containers do not survive this — instruments lose precision within months.</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-900 font-semibold mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-gray-200">Planexus response: F9 pre-filter, cooling load +35 °C, pad-foundation engineering from the factory.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- STRATEGISCHE FUSION INTRO -->
    <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-slate-50">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-8 text-slate-900">
            Lab containers for Stuttgart: what the basin climate, Section 50 LBO BW and industrial density demand of the engineering
          </h2>
          <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6">
            <p>
              <strong>Stuttgart is Germany’s densest cluster for powertrain research, precision mechanics, materials analytics and sensor technology.</strong> In the tightest of spaces, the sports-car industry, tier-1 suppliers, materials laboratories, laser technology and a dense network of university and research campuses compete for land, permits and engineering capacity. Anyone ordering a container laboratory here is not buying a standard product — they are buying site intelligence.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>We know this market in detail.</strong> We know that the basin inversion with fine-dust peaks of up to 50 µg/m³ at Neckartor forces F9 pre-filtration in the HVAC. We know that lithium-ion and powertrain research in Untertürkheim and Zuffenhausen requires ATEX Zone 1. We know that the Filder plain needs pad-foundation structural design to soil class 4, and that the Vaihingen university campus requires vibration isolation for optics and laser technology. These details are not in our quotation — they are the engineering foundation of every container that leaves our Albstadt works.
            </p>
            <p>
              <strong>The shortest distance is our strongest competitive advantage.</strong> 80 kilometres. 1.5 hours of heavy-goods transport via the A81. Same-day delivery possible. A factory visit in under two hours — from either side. No northern German, NRW or Hessian supplier can offer that for Stuttgart.
            </p>
            <p>
              Whether you need a <strong>mobile laboratory Stuttgart</strong> for a time-limited third-party-funded campaign, a <strong>modular lab container Stuttgart</strong> for a permanent factory expansion in Feuerbach, or a <strong>container laboratory Stuttgart</strong> with BSL-2 containment for the university hospital — we deliver all three answers from the same platform: the LABtoGO from our Albstadt works.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 6 PLANEXUS-LEISTUNGEN STUTTGART (Service-Region-Fusion) -->
    <section class="py-16 md:py-24">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
          <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-14">
            <div class="text-primary font-bold text-sm uppercase tracking-wider mb-3">Services for Stuttgart</div>
